-- Layer consumption sweep
--
-- One axiom report for every public declaration in `Hypermath/`, so that
-- the layer stack's shape is measured rather than asserted. A report
-- names two different kinds of thing: the Lean foundation axioms a proof
-- costs, and the repository's own declared symbols and clauses it uses.
-- The second is what this file is for. Together the reports say which
-- layer's declarations each layer's content actually consumes, and which
-- declared clauses nothing consumes at all.
--
-- Generated from the sources; `test_the_sweep_covers_every_public_declaration`
-- regenerates the list and requires it to match, so a new declaration
-- cannot quietly escape the measurement.

